# Owner's native MacBook session and Tailscale connection require the real phone.
[phone] Open a native Claude Code conversation on the MacBook, with one prompt and visible reply; keep the existing native Codex session.
[phone] With no Soma-owned work running or waiting, deploy and restart the updated MacBook runner.
[phone] In Soma Sessions select MacBook Pro: within two scan periods the already-open Claude conversation must appear alongside Codex. Capture the session list screenshot.
[phone] Open that Claude conversation: verify prompt/reply and the read-only mirror note; no thinking, tool-result payloads or subagent conversations appear. Capture screenshot.
[phone] Continue in Claude Code on the Mac: verify new visible text appears once in Soma without a duplicate session.
[phone] Try replying from Soma: verify the Mac-only reply explanation, no new Claude process and no duplicate user message; continue normally in Claude Code on the Mac.
[phone] Restart the idle runner again: verify the same session and no repeated messages. Capture screenshot.
